  "interpretation": [
    "Mono long-exposure p95 rises from 87.28ms to 469.57ms (5.38x): the old scene retained 300 objects, while the new geometry considers 8,920 candidates and retains a median 4,183.5 sources over 25,202.5 temporal samples. Source prediction and rendering visit about 3.23m and 3.21m kernel cells respectively. Median capture CPU rises from 91.47ms to 293.17ms; measured projection/prediction/reference/render CPU is 31.76/60.56/2.70/135.83ms.",
    "Short Mono renders fewer admitted sources but evaluates thousands of complete candidates and their aperture predictions before rejecting them. All Mono cases allocate more than the old 300-object route; the raw comparison records those costs rather than claiming an unchanged workload.",
    "CFA short p95 improves (0.78x); other CFA/ASI676 cases range from 1.04x to 1.95x. Highest measured cumulative process peak is 1.787GiB, from ASI676 short. All nine predeclared budgets pass. These results do not prove ARM resource qualification or real hardware behavior."
  ]
